@page
@model TonesModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Tones";
}

<h1>Tones guide</h1>
<p class="lead">Mandarin has four tones plus a neutral tone. The same syllable means different things depending on its tone.</p>

<div class="row g-3 mb-4">
    @foreach (var t in Model.Tones)
    {
        <div class="col-md-4 col-lg">
            <div class="card h-100 text-center tone-@t.Number"><div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">@t.Name</h5>
                <div class="display-4">@t.Mark</div>
                <p class="small">@t.Description</p>
                <div class="hanzi fs-2">@t.Hanzi</div>
                <div class="pinyin">@t.Example — @t.Meaning</div>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary mt-2 speak" data-text="@t.Hanzi">🔊 Listen</button>
            </div></div>
        </div>
    }
</div>

<h3>Tone change rules</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Two 3rd tones in a row:</strong> the first becomes 2nd tone. 你好 nǐ hǎo is said <em>ní hǎo</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>不 bù:</strong> becomes 2nd tone before a 4th tone. 不是 is said <em>bú shì</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>一 yī:</strong> becomes 4th tone before tones 1–3 (一天 <em>yì tiān</em>) and 2nd tone before a 4th tone (一个 <em>yí ge</em>).</li>
</ul>

<h3>Where does the tone mark go?</h3>
<ol>
    <li>If there's an <strong>a</strong> or <strong>e</strong>, it takes the mark: hǎo, xiè.</li>
    <li>In <strong>ou</strong>, the <strong>o</strong> takes it: dōu.</li>
    <li>Otherwise the last vowel takes it: guì, liù.</li>
</ol>
